EXT. GHOST TOWN - DEAD FERRY LANDING - DUSK

A dry riverbed. A rotting dock with no water beneath it. Wind in a broken pilot-house. A weathered sign: LAST CROSSING.

SHERIFF MORDECAI WELLS, 50s, bone-thin, gray coat. A tin star gone dull. He stands at the end of the pier, hat tipped back.

CALISTA REYNOSO, 20s, a bounty hunter in dusty leathers. Scarred cheek. Dual pistols. She sits on a barrel, legs swinging.

PRESTON GRIGGS, 40s, in irons, wrists chained, face swollen. He kneels on the planks.

A radio set crackles from a saddlebag.

WELLS
You said the river was here.

CALISTA
It was here.

WELLS
Where is it now?

CALISTA
Went to Mexico, I guess.

Griggs laughs, a raw cough.

GRIGGS
Told you. Told you both.

WELLS
Shut him up.

CALISTA
He's tired.

GRIGGS
Tired. That's the word.

The radio spits static. A woman's voice, faint.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Sheriff Wells, come in. Sheriff Wells.

Wells crosses the dock. Lifts the receiver.

WELLS
This is Wells.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Mordecai. The judge says to bring him in alive.

WELLS
Understood.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Alive. You hear?

WELLS
I heard.

He sets the receiver down. Turns.

CALISTA
Well?

WELLS
Judge wants him breathing.

CALISTA
Judge isn't here.

GRIGGS
(smiling)
There it is.

Wells pulls his revolver. Calista lays a hand on one of hers. The wind kicks up dust. A loose plank bangs somewhere. Nobody moves.

WELLS
We take him in at dawn.

CALISTA
And tonight?

WELLS
We sit.

He holsters the gun. Sits on the dock edge, legs over the dry bed. After a moment, Calista joins him. Griggs, between them, lowers his head.
